# Evidence, lock files, fixtures and manifests are verified by SHA-256 over
# their exact bytes. With core.autocrlf=true (Windows) git rewrites LF to CRLF
# in the working copy, so a recorded hash stops matching the file on disk.
# Core/.gitattributes pins only two dataset cards and hit this problem.
# Pin text files to LF here; keep binary artifacts free of any conversion.
# One pattern per line: gitattributes does not accept several patterns on a line.
* text=auto

*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.pro text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary artifacts: no EOL conversion, no text diff or merge.
*.aar binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.onnx binary
*.ort binary
*.wav binary
*.bz2 binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
